{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadMajorantRate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadMajorantRate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadLinkScaffold","lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddleClausen"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLink_volume_of_lemma4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLink_volume_of_lemma4","kind":"theorem","line":784,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L784-L795","doc":"**The Whitehead-link volume limit, conditional ONLY on vdV Lemma 4.**\nWith the majorant rate discharged sorry-free (W6), the scaffold's\nconditional squeeze needs nothing but the named `VdVWhiteheadLemma4`\nclass: `(2π/N)·log ‖J_N(W)‖ → 4·Cl₂(π/2) = 4G = Vol(L5a1)`.  The\nGaussian/erfc non-cancellation is now the SOLE open input on the\n`b = 1` front. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_whiteheadLinkMajorant_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_whiteheadLinkMajorant_vol","kind":"theorem","line":767,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L767-L782","doc":"The majorant rate in `Vol_Borromean/2 = 4G` form — the exact input shape\nof the scaffold's conditional squeeze. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_two_pi_log_whiteheadLinkMajorant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_two_pi_log_whiteheadLinkMajorant","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L482-L765","doc":"**W6c — the majorant volume rate (sorry-free).**  The phase-free\nWhitehead-link majorant obeys the volume growth law:\n`(2π/N)·log(whiteheadLinkMajorant N) → 4·clausen(π/2) = 4G`.  Upper\nenvelope: at most `2N³` terms, each below the W6b ceiling; lower\nenvelope: the single grid term at `(⌊N/2⌋, ⌊N/4⌋)`, whose deviation\ntarget converges to the saddle value by continuity of `clausen`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLink_term_ceiling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLink_term_ceiling","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L380-L477","doc":"**W6b — the per-term ceiling (sorry-free).**  Every majorant grid term\nobeys `(2π/N)·log S_{n,k} ≤ 4·clausen(π/2) + 10·masterErr N`: interior\nterms by the generic W4b deviation landing exactly on\n`whiteheadFunctional2` (no grid-shift slack), the `n = 0` row by\n`S_{0,k} = 1`, the `k = 0` column by the bare `s_n` deviation plus\nantisymmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm_zero_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm_zero_left","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L372-L377","doc":"The empty window: `S_{0,k} = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional2_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional2_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L358-L368","doc":"The saddle value: `g(π, π/2) = 4·clausen(π/2)` (antisymmetry at `3π/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional2_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional2_le","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L318-L356","doc":"**W6a — the 2D continuum max (sorry-free, no compactness).**  On the\ntriangle `{u,v ≥ 0, u+v ≤ 2π}` the functional never exceeds its saddle\nvalue `4·clausen(π/2) = 4G`, attained at `(π, π/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional2","kind":"def","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L312-L316","doc":"The van der Veen 2-variable functional in clausen coordinates:\n`g(u,v) = clausen u + 2·clausen v − 2·clausen(u+v)` — the continuum\nlimit of `(2π/N)·log S_{n,k}` along `2πn/N → u`, `2πk/N → v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadPsi1D_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadPsi1D_le","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L269-L308","doc":"**The ψ brick.**  `ψ(u) = clausen u + 4·clausen(π − u/2)` is monotone on\n`[0, π]` (same derivative sign as ρ after `sin(π/2 − u/4) = cos(u/4)`),\nso it is at most its endpoint value `ψ(π) = 4·clausen(π/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadRho_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadRho_le","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L228-L267","doc":"**The ρ brick.**  `ρ(c) = 4·clausen(c/2) − clausen c` is monotone on\n`[0, π]` (derivative `log(2cos(c/4)) − log(2sin(c/4)) ≥ 0`), so it is at\nmost its endpoint value `ρ(π) = 4·clausen(π/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_sin_quarter_le_log_cos_quarter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_sin_quarter_le_log_cos_quarter","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L213-L226","doc":"The shared derivative sign: `log(2 cos(x/4)) ≥ log(2 sin(x/4))` for\n`0 < x ≤ π` (i.e. `x/4 ≤ π/4`, where sine is below cosine). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_two_sin_half_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_two_sin_half_split","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L197-L211","doc":"Double-angle log split: `log(2 sin(x/2)) = log(2 sin(x/4)) + log(2 cos(x/4))`\nfor `0 < x < 2π` (both factors positive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.clausen_pair_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.clausen_pair_le","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L136-L195","doc":"**Symmetric-pair brick.**  For `0 ≤ v ≤ c ≤ π`,\n`clausen v + clausen(c−v) ≤ 2·clausen(c/2)` — the symmetric sum peaks at\nthe midpoint (monotone on `[0, c/2]` since\n`sin(t/2) ≤ sin((c−t)/2)` there, then reflect). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.clausen_le_double_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.clausen_le_double_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L109-L134","doc":"`clausen` never exceeds twice its saddle value on `[0, 2π]`:\n`clausen y ≤ 2·clausen(π/2)`.  On `[0, π]` this is the sibling brick\n`clausen_diff_le` plus `clausen(y+π) = −clausen(π−y) ≤ 0`; on `[π, 2π]`\nthe function is `≤ 0` by antisymmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.clausen_two_pi_sub_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.clausen_two_pi_sub_eq","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadMajorantRate.lean#L90-L107","doc":"Antisymmetry of `clausen` about `π` on `[0, 2π]`:\n`clausen(2π − x) = −clausen x` — the integral-side transport of the\nseries identity `Cl_2_two_pi_sub` through the `clausen = Cl₂` bridge,\nwith the endpoints closed by `clausen_zero` / `clausen_two_pi`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}